# Dual-Word Edge Detection Function Block

Here's a complete ST implementation of the edge detection function block:

```structured-text
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_DualWordEdgeDetection
VAR_OUTPUT
    hasChanged      : BOOL;
    hasRisingEdges  : BOOL;
    risingBits      : DWORD;
    noOfRisingBits  : USINT;
    hasFallingEdges : BOOL;
    fallingBits     : DWORD;
    noOfFallingBits : USINT;
END_VAR

VAR_INPUT
    value : DWORD;
END_VAR

VAR
    prevValue : DWORD;
END_VAR

// ============================================================================
// Internal Function: Count the number of set bits in a DWORD
// Uses Brian Kernighan's algorithm for efficiency
// ============================================================================
FUNCTION PRIVATE FB_CountBits : USINT
VAR_INPUT
    bits : DWORD;
END_VAR
VAR
    count : USINT := 0;
END_VAR
    WHILE bits <> 0 DO
        bits := bits & (bits - 1);
        count := count + 1;
    END_WHILE
    FB_CountBits := count;
END_FUNCTION

// ============================================================================
// Main Edge Detection Logic
// ============================================================================

// Rising edge detection: current = 1 AND previous = 0
risingBits := value AND (NOT prevValue);

// Falling edge detection: current = 0 AND previous = 1
fallingBits := (NOT value) AND prevValue;

// Check if the entire value has changed
hasChanged := (value <> prevValue);

// Set boolean flags for edge detection
hasRisingEdges  := (risingBits <> 16#00000000);
hasFallingEdges := (fallingBits <> 16#00000000);

// Count the number of set bits (edges) in each pattern
noOfRisingBits  := FB_CountBits(risingBits);
noOfFallingBits := FB_CountBits(fallingBits);

// Store current value for next cycle edge detection
prevValue := value;

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
```

## How It Works

| Operation | Formula | Description |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| **Rising Edge** | `value AND NOT prevValue` | Bit is 1 now, was 0 before |
| **Falling Edge** | `NOT value AND prevValue` | Bit is 0 now, was 1 before |
| **Changed** | `value <> prevValue` | Any bit difference |
| **Bit Counting** | Brian Kernighan's algorithm | Efficiently counts set bits |

## Usage Example

```structured-text
PROGRAM Example
VAR
    detector : FB_DualWordEdgeDetection;
    inputVal : DWORD := 16#00000000;
END_VAR

// Call the function block
detector(value := inputVal);

// Check outputs
IF detector.hasChanged THEN
    ; // Value has changed
END_IF

IF detector.hasRisingEdges THEN
    ; // At least one bit transitioned from 0 to 1
    // detector.risingBits shows which bits
    // detector.noOfRisingBits shows how many
END_IF

IF detector.hasFallingEdges THEN
    ; // At least one bit transitioned from 1 to 0
    // detector.fallingBits shows which bits
    // detector.noOfFallingBits shows how many
END_IF

// Update input for next cycle
inputVal := some_new_value;
END_PROGRAM
```

